d that one's identity gives  them valuable perspective but it can go  too far and when identity becomes a  trump card to silence debate and say  none of your opinions matter because of  my identity and what I have to say  that's a major problem and I've called  it out it's not a gigantic problem on  the left but it exists and I call it out  when I see it all of this leads us to  yesterday when Amy Susskind a notable  feminist activist tweeted the following  quote I will not support white male  candidates in the Democratic primary  unless you slept through the midterms  women were our most successful candidate  biggest dem voters the biggest demo'd  getters in history Obama oh eight  Hillary sixteen white male is not where  our party is at and is our least safe  option in 2020 this is exactly the stuff  that we need to condemn and putting  aside the fact that you would expect  that over time candidates would get more  and more votes because the population  keeps growing like that's a completely  meaningless statement that Obama and  Hillary got record number of votes so  from Democrats  we need to condemn this because of the  idea and I immediately tweeted Amy back  and got a lot of people who agreed with  me and some people who disagreed and  said isn't there something not  progressive about preemptively  dismissing a candidate based on their  race and gender I feel like there's a  word to describe that as a progressive I  won't be jumping on board with that idea  ideas experience ability perspective  issues no she is saying no white men  this is racism and this is sexism so Amy  Siskind started getting crushed by some  on the left for what she said and the  right immediately started holding her up  exactly what they want us to be  portrayed as which is completely  self-destructive for us right so  whatever she meant by this even if we  charitably attribute to her that what  she meant was Oh what I mean is I think  a non someone who's not a white male is  more likely to win okay if that's what  she meant she said it in the worst  possible way and it makes us look  absolutely terrible so the left needs to  make it like crystal clear that this  stuff cannot be tolerated  it cannot be toyed with it cannot be  entertained period and you know Pat it  is a small percentage of the left but  like Jonathan Hite said it has the  effect of it being a much larger  percentage of the left because of how  the right will seize on this nonsense  and crush us for it we can't have this  stuff we just can't have it policy  positions have to be number one after  that you can look at things like  character and values and identity comes  far after that and I think this logic is  just silly at the end of the day and it  gets really wishy-washy to like does she  discount Bernie Sanders he is a white  man but he's also Jewish so that's a  minority at some periods of time in  history Jews were not considered white  so I'm not sure if he's allowed to be  supported by her or someone like beta  Roark who is Irish American but hey he  has a Hispanic nickname and he speaks  Spanish so is that acceptable I think  this is just a really silly conversation  to have it's completely silly it's  completely counterproductive and that's  exactly the problem as soon as you start  saying this is how you will evaluate  candidates you get into stuff like okay  well Jews are an extreme minority but  they're often characterized as having  the same white privilege because they  pass as white but at the same time  anti-semitism is rampant so what do you  do with Bernie right immediately this is  why you got to get away from this stuff  it should be condemned if I'm missing  something let me know I really want to  hear from you if you think I'm missing  something  today's program is sponsored in part by  Blink asam / Pakman if you've not  already heard about blink Asst it's  amazing it's an app for your phone  tablet or web browser and what they do  is they take nonfiction books popular  nonfiction critically acclaimed  nonfiction they condense the book into a  fifteen minute audio book you get all  the most important information and  insights from each book but you can soak  up the entire essence of the book in one  sitting I've listened to a ton of books  on blankest one recent one is a Robert  Rice's new book the common good also  bunk by Kevin Young useful in preparing  me for the pseudo-science miniseries  that we're producing and if you are a  david pakman show viewer or listener you  can get a seven day free trial by going  to blink accom slash Pakman if you're  watching on youtube use the link in the  video description  after the free trial if you like it you  can get the full access to thousands of  condensed audiobooks for about five  bucks a month that's be li NK is t.com  /pa ke ma n
 

